    #536 wiringcliff: two probes wired into gate_arm.sh, eleven exemptions re-dated to 2026-09-27 by owner ruling -- and the checker's selftest derives its dates now
    
    check_probe_wiring.py's EXEMPT table carried thirteen entries dated 2026-09-20; the
    comparison is d < today, so precommit section R would have hard-failed every
    commit from the 21st.  Owner ruling 2026-09-18: wire the two that are cheap,
    re-date the other eleven to 2026-09-27, each still naming the gate that owes it.
    
    regress/gate_arm.sh -- two sections after the pcc2 c040 section:
      - mk48_nvram_probe.py (#521, 57 rows, sentinel MK48_WITNESS_DONE) on
        mvme88k/mvme187.  Its EXEMPT reason, "no gate drives mvme88k/mvme187", was
        false when written: gate_arm.sh already ran pcc2_width_probe.py (b78bb0f)
        and pcc2_default_probe.py (ecc4d3b) on mvme187.
      - hpcmips_ctor_probe.py (#444, 28 construction IDs, ~8 s) as a construction
        check; the RESULT line is the sentinel, ^HPCMIPS_CTOR_PASS$ the verdict.
        C2 borrows its unrelated-abort control from mvme1600's live PCI defect --
        disclosed in the comment, filed as hpcmipsc2.
    
    tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py
      - EXEMPT: mk48 and hpcmips entries removed; eleven re-dated to 2026-09-27.
      - --selftest M5a/M5b pinned the literals 2026-09-19 / 2026-09-21; with the
        block moved, M5b runs on a tree with nothing expired and the selftest
        fails (21/22 measured).  Both days are now DERIVED from the earliest
        dated detector exemption, and M5a runs ON that date, not the day before:
        the Opus seat measured the day-before form blind to d < today -> d <=
        today (22/22); the stamped-date form catches it (21/22).
      - comments: the fbpending_bound pairing (one half discharged by #537,
        premise in the past tense), M5f, the mk48 MANIFEST note, and the EXEMPT
        block's claim that every probe prints a verdict token and exits nonzero
        -- false of mk48 (agy; ruled L4 by fable5 and corrected in-round).
      - MANIFEST: four CLASS_TOOL lines for this round's apply536_*.py editors.
    tools/precommit_check.sh: section R's comment -- the dates live in the
      checker; "18 mutants" -> the pinned 22; "36 files" -> "when this was written".
    
    Measured (regress/artifacts/wiringcliff/r536_20260918/): checker PASS 70/81 +
    11 dated-exempt; --today 2026-09-26 and 2026-09-27 PASS, 2026-09-28 FAIL naming
    exactly the eleven; --selftest 22/22; the old literal days 21/22 (M5b); a
    d <= today mutant 21/22 (M5a).  The edits commute with the working tree's
    uncommitted #529 hunks (cmp), so #536 ships alone.
    Gate 14 (gate_arm.sh) alone 2026-09-18 23:06-00:30: PASS, 1044 checks,
    0 FAIL; the mk48 section 61 checks and hpcmips 32, all green (log in the
    artifacts dir).  The binary under test carries six uncommitted src/ edits
    of other open rounds, none from #536.
    
    Panel: the same pass 2 + section-F2 as #537 (one brief), nine seats, fable5
